  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The ancient city of Petra, carved into the sandstone cliffs of Jordan, was once a major trading hub in the Middle East. Its strategic location allowed merchants to transport goods between the Mediterranean and the Indian Ocean. The city's impressive architecture, including the iconic Monastery and the Royal Tombs, is a testament to the advanced engineering skills of its builders.\n\nDespite being abandoned for centuries, Petra has recently experienced a resurgence in popularity due to its unique blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Visitors from around the world flock to see the intricate facades, temples, and monuments that adorn the city's narrow canyon streets. The Jordanian government has also invested heavily in preserving the site, recognizing its potential as a major tourist destination.\n\nHowever, critics argue that the influx of tourists is threatening the delicate balance between preservation and commercialization. They claim that the increased foot traffic is causing damage to the fragile structures and disrupting the local ecosystem. Others worry about the impact on the surrounding communities, who are struggling to cope with the sudden influx of visitors.\n\nAs a result, the Jordanian authorities have implemented measures to regulate tourism and protect the site's integrity. These efforts include limiting visitor numbers, enforcing strict rules for photography and exploration, and promoting sustainable practices among tour operators.\n\nDespite these challenges, Petra remains an awe-inspiring destination that continues to captivate the imagination of visitors from around the world.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was the main reason for Petra's decline?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It was abandoned due to a lack of water\", \"The city was destroyed by earthquakes and floods\", \"Petra's strategic location made it vulnerable to attacks from neighboring tribes\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is one of the concerns about the increased tourism in Petra?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The local economy will benefit greatly\", \"The fragile structures are being damaged and the ecosystem disrupted\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the text imply about the author's attitude towards the preservation of Petra?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The author is dismissive of the importance of preserving historical sites\", \"The author believes that commercialization should take precedence over preservation\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What measure has been implemented to regulate tourism in Petra?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Limiting visitor numbers and enforcing strict rules for photography\", \"Promoting sustainable practices among tour operators only\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is one of the benefits of visiting Petra?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The city's unique blend of history and natural beauty\", \"Visitors can explore the surrounding communities without restrictions\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
